import source_navigation.dl
import source_hover.dl

to [open UI source context at] {UI bounds:anchor} [for byte] {integer:position} [in] {a pointer to UI source tools:tools}:
    begin UI source interaction in tools
    set tools's mode to 6
    set tools's position to position
    set tools's context anchor to anchor
    set tools's context revision to tools's document's revision
    set tools's context project revision to tools's document's project's revision
    set tools's choices' preferred width to 276.0
    set tools's choices' on release to true
    add UI choice (the string form of "Go to definition (F12)") enabled true to (the address of (tools's choices))
    set tools's choices' last item's icon to "link"
    show UI choice popover (the address of (tools's choices)) reporting "" with hint "" in (tools's view)

to get [read UI source context in] {a pointer to UI source tools:tools}:
    set view to tools's view
    if (tools's mode = 6) and (view's input kind = 5):
        if ((the UI cursor in view) is inside (tools's choices' bounds)) = false:
            dismiss UI source tools tools
    if (view's input kind != 2) or (view's input code != 3):
        return false
    if tools's mode = 6:
        dismiss UI source tools tools
    set point to the UI cursor in view
    set layout to the UI hit at point in view
    if layout = (0 as a pointer to UI layout):
        return false
    set editor to (tools's workspace as a pointer to UI source workspace)'s editors
    loop while editor != (0 as a pointer to UI source editor):
        if editor's node = layout's node:
            return open UI source pointer context for editor at point in tools
        set editor to editor's next
    return false

to get [open UI source pointer context for] {a pointer to UI source editor:editor} [at] {UI point:point} [in] {a pointer to UI source tools:tools}:
    set view to tools's view
    if editor's workspace's client's phase = 8:
        return false
    if (editor's document's available = false) or ((the UI element (editor's node) is enabled in (view's instance)) = false):
        return false
    set run to the UI text hit at point in view
    set position to -1
    if run != (0 as a pointer to UI text run):
        if run's source's element = editor's node:
            set position to the UI source byte under point in run
    remember the UI source location of editor in view
    if position >= 0:
        if (position < (the minimum of (editor's current's anchor) and (editor's current's caret))) or (position > (the maximum of (editor's current's anchor) and (editor's current's caret))):
            set editor's current's anchor and editor's current's caret to position
    restore UI source location (editor's current) in editor in view
    require condition (focus UI source tools tools) reporting "The context menu could not focus its source editor"
    open UI source context at (UI box at (point's x) (point's y) sized 1 1) for byte position in tools
    set tools's choices' first item's enabled to position >= 0
    if position < 0:
        set tools's choices' selected to -1
    return true

to [accept UI source context in] {a pointer to UI source tools:tools}:
    set editor to the UI source editor in tools
    set editor's current's anchor and editor's current's caret to tools's position
    restore UI source location (editor's current) in editor in (tools's view)
    request a UI source definition in tools
